      en: "Black Mountain Pass is a remote mountain pass in eastern Lesotho, near the border with South Africa's KwaZulu-Natal province. It reaches an elevation of 2,600 m (8,530 ft) and is a gravel road used primarily by 4x4 vehicles. The pass connects the isolated valleys of Mokhotlong and Matatiele. The area is known for dense fog and sudden weather changes. The name derives from the dark basalt rocks that dominate the landscape. The road is seasonal and often closed in winter. The pass offers dramatic views of the Drakensberg peaks. Nearby are several alpine lakes. The region is a key refuge for the bearded vulture.",
